From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jesse Zhang <Jesse.Zhang@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:56:33 +0800
Subject: drm/amdgpu: complete the guilty fence at the end of a multi ring reset

amdgpu_ring_backup_unprocessed_commands() skips the backup of a ring and
clears ring->guilty_fence when it sees the same guilty fence again, to
avoid replay loops. That happens when the IP block soft reset follows a
failed ring reset of the same job. amdgpu_multi_ring_reset_helper_end()
then restored the guilty ring with ring->guilty_fence, NULL by then, so
neither the guilty fence nor the rest of the ring was completed: the hung
job stayed pending until it timed out again.

Pass the guilty fence to the end helper, and use it for the guilty ring.
For the other rings, and when the backup didn't drop it, nothing changes.

Signed-off-by: Jesse Zhang <Jesse.Zhang@amd.com>

[ORDER 525: carried from amd-gfx, not merged upstream (v3 02/15 of 2026-10-28).
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/amd-gfx/20261028085736.3808569-2-Jesse.Zhang@amd.com/
Why this kernel needs it: on 7.3.1-stereo3d16 the A10's Radeon R5 M430 (Hainan, gfx_v6_0, no wave-kill soft recovery) wedged after a WebGPU compute job ran past the 2000 ms watchdog: the IP block soft reset reported success every 3.5 s for the same fence (signaled 90991, emitted 90992) and never completed it, so the browser, TTM's delayed-delete workers and every waiter on that fence slept in D state until a reboot. The devcoredump of the loop shows the restored ring: init, clear state, two ring tests, then only NOP padding (Rptr == Wptr), no EVENT_WRITE_EOP for 90992. On gfx6 no ring reset precedes the soft reset; the repeat comes from the same fence timing out again after a soft reset (or from a later fence allocated at the address ring->guilty_fence still holds), and the end helper got NULL for it every second cycle.
Adapted to v7.3.1 only in its hunks: v3 01/15 ("pass the device to the multi ring reset helpers") is not carried, so the end helper keeps taking the device from guilty_ring; the changed lines are the same.
In v4 of the series (2026-11-05) this patch was replaced by Timur Kristóf's "drm/amdgpu/ring: During multi-queue reset, only call begin helper if needed" (v4 02/13), which keeps the first backup and replays it on every repeat; on gfx6, where the repeat is not a failed ring reset, a replay that does not complete then loops the same way, and a stale ring->guilty_fence makes it replay another job's old backup. This patch completes the fence on a repeat instead (-ETIME for it, -ECANCELED for the rest of the ring), as ce3f23a78085 and 930a915de89c intended ("If we've already seen a fence, don't backup the ring contents since presumably either the previous reset was not successful or there was something wrong with the data").
Drop this group when either form, or another fix that completes a repeated guilty fence after an IP block soft reset, reaches the release this kernel moves to.]
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ip.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ip.c
index 922f4b1..cee758d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ip.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ip.c
@@ -511,7 +511,8 @@ int amdgpu_device_ip_soft_reset(struct amdgpu_ring *guilty_ring,
 
 	r = ip_block->version->funcs->soft_reset(ip_block);
 
-	r = amdgpu_multi_ring_reset_helper_end(ring_type_mask, guilty_ring, r);
+	r = amdgpu_multi_ring_reset_helper_end(ring_type_mask, guilty_ring,
+					       guilty_fence, r);
 	amdgpu_device_unlock_reset_domain(adev->reset_domain);
 
 	if (r) {
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ring.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ring.c
index 5922406..97e09af 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ring.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ring.c
@@ -1055,6 +1055,7 @@ void amdgpu_multi_ring_reset_helper_begin(const u32 ring_type_mask,
  *
  * @ring_type_mask: Bitmask of affected ring types
  * @guilty_ring: The ring which is guilty of causing a reset.
+ * @guilty_fence: The fence which didn't signal on the guilty ring.
  * @ret: Return code from the reset function.
  *
  * After calling amdgpu_multi_ring_reset_helper_begin()
@@ -1066,7 +1067,8 @@ void amdgpu_multi_ring_reset_helper_begin(const u32 ring_type_mask,
  * fully restore the ring contents.
  */
 int amdgpu_multi_ring_reset_helper_end(const u32 ring_type_mask,
-				       struct amdgpu_ring *guilty_ring, int ret)
+				       struct amdgpu_ring *guilty_ring,
+				       struct amdgpu_fence *guilty_fence, int ret)
 {
 	struct amdgpu_device *adev = guilty_ring->adev;
 	struct amdgpu_ring *ring;
@@ -1097,8 +1099,13 @@ int amdgpu_multi_ring_reset_helper_end(const u32 ring_type_mask,
 		if (!(BIT(ring->funcs->type) & ring_type_mask))
 			continue;
 
-		/* Restore contents of the ring */
-		r = amdgpu_ring_reset_helper_end(ring, ring->guilty_fence);
+		/*
+		 * Restore contents of the ring. The backup of the guilty ring
+		 * may have dropped its guilty fence, eg. after a failed ring
+		 * reset with the same fence: still complete it.
+		 */
+		r = amdgpu_ring_reset_helper_end(ring, ring == guilty_ring ?
+						 guilty_fence : ring->guilty_fence);
 		if (r) {
 			dev_err(adev->dev,
 				"Failed to recover ring %s after soft reset\n",
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ring.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ring.h
index 015623b..ed4fcac 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ring.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ring.h
@@ -599,7 +599,8 @@ void amdgpu_multi_ring_reset_helper_begin(const u32 ring_type_mask,
 					  struct amdgpu_ring *guilty_ring,
 					  struct amdgpu_fence *guilty_fence);
 int amdgpu_multi_ring_reset_helper_end(const u32 ring_type_mask,
-				       struct amdgpu_ring *guilty_ring, int ret);
+				       struct amdgpu_ring *guilty_ring,
+				       struct amdgpu_fence *guilty_fence, int ret);
 bool amdgpu_ring_is_reset_type_supported(struct amdgpu_ring *ring,
 					 u32 reset_type);
 #endif
